    "updated_at": "2020-12-01T09:24:48Z",
    "body": "Hi @mickimnet, thanks for mentioning the helpful discussion!\r\n\r\nThis is my new config, it works! But, unfortunately very slowly.\r\n```toml\r\n[custom.bash]\r\ncommand = \"echo Bash \"\r\nwhen = \"\"\" test \"$STARSHIP_SHELL\" \"==\" \"bash\" \"\"\"\r\nformat = \"$output\"\r\n\r\n[custom.pwsh]\r\ncommand = \"echo pwsh \"\r\nwhen = \"\"\" \"$env:STARSHIP_SHELL\" -eq \"powershell\" \"\"\"\r\nformat = \"$output\"\r\n```\r\nWhen I use PowerShell, this configuration led to about 2 seconds of latency. I think this is probably because PowerShell also checks the \"when\" condition `test \"$STARSHIP_SHELL\" \"==\" \"bash\" ` But, PowerShell doesn't have \"test\" cmdlet or function. So starship got stuck there. ",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
